272	 * BENNY. The approved picture holds only ~50 u of river and only its first ~10 u (around Benny) at full sharpness; laid
273	 * onto the world, riding forward magnified far rows into a blurred sheet, and the near tile T2 that took over is a
274	 * repeated patch (centre in-painted under Benny) that read as marbled swirls without the painted S-bands. Under the
275	 * switch every projection layer (E, N, T, T2, flow maps, detail) is read at s − (ride s − locked s): a point d units
276	 * ahead of Benny shows the approved water that lies d units ahead of Benny in the approved picture, so the S-shaped
277	 * pink banks, cyan middle and glossy streaks keep their painted size and sharpness while swimming, on the real river
278	 * geometry (lateral position u stays the world's: steering shows the other parts of the painted river). The two-phase
279	 * flow still slides the streaks toward the camera. At the locked checkpoint the offset is 0 → the picture is unchanged.
280	 */
281	export const M05RIDE: boolean = TGTWALL05 && q05('m05ride');
282	/**
283	 * `&m05seam=1` (Screen 05 round 8, needs m05ride + m05far): the near river meets the far tunnel's river at the sliding
284	 * seam. With m05ride the near river shows the approved design Benny-relative, so once the seam stops sliding (capped
285	 * just before 06, Benny ≈ 139 on) the near river reached the seam with design rows from the approved MIDDLE distance
286	 * while the far river continues the approved picture's LAST near-river rows: the pink / cyan bands broke in a step line
287	 * across the river. Over the stretch before the seam (60 % of Benny → seam, 4–20 u) the design is eased (quadratic, no
288	 * kink) so it arrives at E's last rows exactly at the seam, as in the locked view. `m05seam.value` = (seam s, live) is
289	 * written every frame by src/world/match05far.ts; locked view and the 06 fold: live = 0, nothing changes.
290	 */
